  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Wednesday/... Confidence is growing\nin a set up to bring warmer temperatures to the southern \npanhandle, Hyder in particular, through the beginning of next \nweek. Sunday is expected to be dry with clearing skies through \nthe day across the entire area before rain chances increase again \nfrom Yakutat northward on Monday. The rest of the panhandle is \nanticipated to remain dry with sunnier skies, which will be the \ndeciding factor in how warm temperatures will get. Cloudier skies \nthen look to move into the northern panhandle on Tuesday, which \nwill cause temperature to remain slightly cooler than Monday's. \nHowever, Wednesday is anticipated to be the warmest day next week \nin the central and southern panhandle given that skies remain \nclear to allow for optimal daytime heating.",
